The two-point average and single uniformly retained point are conditionally unbiased, but their variances are 1/2 and 1. Therefore unbiasedness does not imply exchangeability. A sufficient validity condition is equivariance in distribution of the entire compression kernel, including allocation, weights, fitted hyperparameters and randomness, under the permutation group. Independent seeds are sufficient in common constructions but not necessary; exchangeable shared randomness may also be valid.

